    "site_desc": "Upland decduous broadleaf forest.  Mainly sugar maple, also basswood.  Uniform stand atop a very modest hill.  Clearcut approximately 80 years ago.  Chosen to be representative of the upland deciduous broadleaf forests within the US-PFa tall tower flux footprint.  It appears to be more heavily forested and more productive than most of the upland deciduous broadleaf forests in the region. Extensive forest thinning in 2013-2014 removed 30% of overstory biomass in flux footprint.",
